<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (In this practical, I learned about the two most important memory systems of a computer: RAM and Storage. RAM is a temporary memory that helps the computer run active programs smoothly, while storage is a permanent memory that keeps data even when the system is turned off.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (I also studied different generations of RAM such as DDR3, DDR4 and DDR5, and understood that each generation has different speed, voltage and compatibility. Similarly, I learned about different storage types like HDD, SSD and NVMe SSD, where HDD is slower but cheaper, SSD is faster, and NVMe SSD provides the highest performance.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Overall, this practical helped me understand how computer performance depends on both RAM and storage working together. RAM handles current tasks, while storage keeps all data safe for long-term use.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
